WEBVTT

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.180
Okay...

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.230
I need to pull up the weeds 
in this yard today.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:20.290
Um... Was that little house there before?

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:24.730
What a nice morning!

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:28.890
Oh, Takeru! Good morning!

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.800
Meow! I'm so embarrassed 
to be seen like this!

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.470
My house is an illegal construction now!

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:39.720
<b>Dragon</b>

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.720
This is my house. Dora-tan used 
Sol/Lull to make it for me!

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.220
It's really amazing!

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.230
Yeah, it's amazing, 
but that's not the point!

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:10.710
<b>ETOTAMA</b>

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:36.760
<b>Episode 3: Reckless Heart</b>

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.670
So, um, I might as well ask...

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.070
What is this about?

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:37.260
<b>This</b>

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:37.760
<b>This</b>

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:38.260
<b>This</b>

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.650
I had Dora-tan build it while

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:44.390
she was fixing your house 
between episodes 1 and 2.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:48.490
It's my apology for destroying 
your house with my Sol/Lull.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:50.880
That doesn't work as an apology at all.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.370
By the way, this is where I'm living now.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.190
The basement?!

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:55.820
It's a bonus apology.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.480
I didn't need a bonus.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.620
They aren't taking away 
from your living space.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:01.970
What's the problem?

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:03.780
That's true, but...

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.690
You didn't say anything 
about it in episode 2,

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.170
so I thought it was okay...

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.040
Right, right.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.710
Wait, you keep saying 
"episode 1" and "episode 2."

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:12.920
What are you talking about?

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.360
Oh, don't worry about that.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.090
Right, right.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.380
Leave breakfast 
to me! Meow!

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.090
Come to think of it, you haven't

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:21.850
gone out to the yard since 
the house was fixed.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.800
You're right, I haven't...

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.140
Well, all right.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.670
Meow yeah!

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:39.660
Now that I have your approval, Takeru,

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.070
I'm ready to buy furniture for my new home!

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.370
Fidget, fidget...

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.950
Can't you have Dora-tan 
make that for you, too?

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.900
Fidget, fidget...

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.900
Wouldn't it be more of a fun event if

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.760
the two of you shopped together?

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:54.370
Fidget, fidget...

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.820
It's an activity for IRL happiness.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:56.120
I don't think that would be fun for me.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.340
Aww!

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.600
I want to shop with you, Takeru!

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.280
Isn't there anything you need?

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.750
Not on the spur of the moment like this...

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.750
I wanna go shopping!

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.260
Oh, that's right. 
I think I'm out of sesame oil.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.510
Th-That's an emergency!

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:17.240
Hurry! Quickly! We have to 
go buy some right now!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.980
You're really psyched up for this...

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.700
Sesame oil is the treasure of humankind.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.530
You're not a human.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:26.940
In the face of sesame oil,

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.200
such details are no more 
significant than a sesame seed!

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.550
You've got nothing but 
sesame oil on the brain.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.450
Shopping!

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:37.890
Furniture!

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:39.200
Shopping!

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:39.710
Sesame!

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:40.970
Shopping!

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:41.540
Sesame!

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:42.720
Shopping!

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.720
Nya-tan, didn't you say you 
wanted to buy furniture?

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:43.310
Sesame!

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.480
Shopping!

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:45.380
Sesame!

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.640
Furniture and appliances 
are the same thing!

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.610
How are they the same?

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:50.970
You're not listening...

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:57.020
I like this one! I'll take it!

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:00.320
It's pretty expensive. Is that okay?

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.980
That's no problem!

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.620
Despite appearances, 
I love keeping things clean.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.070
I'm totally confident that I can 
use this washing machine's specs

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:08.570
to their fullest!

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:12.080
No, I mean, can you afford it?

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.330
Yep, yep, yep, yep.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.640
It's okay!

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:25.720
I just have to go ask for 
an advance on my paycheck!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.090
Huh? You work? I'm surprised.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.590
Heh!

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.850
This is where I work part-time. 
Maid Café Eto!

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.890
Everyone working hard?

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:44.930
Huh? What are the Eto-shin doing here?

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.900
They all work at this café.

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:48.710
They work?

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:51.660
Isn't Sol/Lull all they need?

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:54.280
Sol/Lull and money are 
two different things.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:56.400
The more money you have, the better.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.790
It never gets in the way.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.280
Right, Shar-tan?

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.260
Yes.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:02.040
She's playing the stock market!

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.920
For me, it's a piece of cake.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:04.210
<b>Remaining 2</b>
This year's hot item: lucky bags! 
Get them before they're gone!

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.720
<b>For Good Luck! Special Lucky Bags</b>

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.720
<b>Limited Time: One Week Only!</b>

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.720
Just as planned, the lucky 
bags have sold out!

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:07.720
<b>Sold Out!</b>

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.090
She's wallowing in greed!

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:12.040
Humans, gods, and Eto-shin 
aren't all that different.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:13.030
Yep, yep.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:13.930
Now...

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.430
I'm here today to get an 
advance on my paycheck.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:21.730
I'll just take about three months' worth!

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:25.730
It won't open...

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:40.250
It exploded?!

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.170
Oh, and something came out!

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:45.570
I'll open it with thi—

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.070
That's a crime.

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:50.380
Property damage and theft.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:53.680
No! I'm just taking my pay!

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.570
That's not happenin'.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:56.450
Why?!

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:00.750
I've never seen you work a single day here.

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:02.480
That's right.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.730
You rolled in here last 
month as a part-timer,

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.730
Roll, roll...

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:08.990
but you just crashed here 
and never did any work.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.200
And you stole food occasionally.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:12.950
Yum!

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:16.850
And she hung all over customers 
with an affinity for cats.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.200
Meow! Cats are so cute, meow!

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.390
She's truly a bad example.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:21.550
No matter how badly she wants Sol/Lull,

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:23.120
at that stage, she's doomed.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.210
That bad?

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:27.250
Th-Th-Th-Then I'll pay it back later!

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.190
Think of it as funding my future—

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:30.260
Meow?

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.360
Manager!

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:33.640
Manager?

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:36.770
I am...

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:39.900
the manager!

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:44.630
Those who do not work shall not get paid!

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.230
<b>Maid Café Eto Manager</b>

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:51.890
Compensation is to be

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:54.700
earned through your blood, 
sweat, and tears!

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:57.760
You dare try to claim it without suffering, 
or even interviewing for it?!

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.200
I won't have it!

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.080
My eyes!

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.620
Absolutely not!

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.600
What intense power of denial!

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.540
And the heat is driving me cra—

00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:06.630
Incidentally, cat-musume!

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.950
I'm the cat Eto-musume! Don't shorten it!

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:10.880
And don't interru—

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:13.160
You should strive to become 
a full-time employee

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:15.010
before becoming one of the zodiac!

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:16.510
A full-time employee?

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:19.690
This is terribly difficult to say, but...

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:23.690
<b>Full-time Employee</b>

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:23.690
What?!

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.760
And why would you deliberately put

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:27.860
your tags in such risqué places?

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:30.690
As for yours, Nya-tan...

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:33.200
<b>Part-time Only</b>

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:36.070
So the truth is that I was 
the only part-timer...

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:40.070
Part-time or full-time makes no 
difference to the customers!

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:42.790
Shut up, you stingy manager!

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:46.710
This is power harassment! 
You're playing favorites!

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.890
Decide your own value

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:51.130
for yourself!

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.240
Thank you for visiting.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:09.890
They've been shunning me! I'm the outcast!

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:12.940
Nya-tan.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:14.320
Meow?

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:15.950
This is your fault.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.570
What? But... But...

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:21.390
No buts.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:25.100
When you've done something wrong, 
you need to show your remorse and apologize.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.260
Sorry.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:31.090
I'm not the one you need to say that to.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:34.970
Okay.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:38.860
Well, ready to go?

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:39.470
Meow?

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.010
You want to buy a washing machine, right?

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:44.810
Yeah!

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.520
<b>Making Preparations</b>

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.520
<b>We're opening at 12:00. Sorry!</b>

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.520
<b>Today's Original Menu:
 Our Special Curry</b>

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.600
Mornin'.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.540
Nya-tan isn't here?

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:55.320
I was certain she'd come 
here trying to get money.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.530
Well, she was here.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.780
She hurled some fightin' words and 
got sent away by the manager.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:03.990
She's so predictable.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:11.790
Was that energy <i>hers</i>?

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:13.800
Yes...

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:19.970
I got this stuff pretty cheap!

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:23.140
Who knew your persuasiveness 
would ever be this useful?

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:31.270
<b>Sesame Oil</b>

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.160
I should've tried to haggle, too.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:29.840
I think you already got a good 
deal by buying industrial size.

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:31.270
That's basic.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:33.710
I bet I could've gotten an

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:35.730
even better deal than that!

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:39.200
You tried to buy a refrigerator 
that way, didn't you?

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.240
With my money.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:44.040
We need a refrigerator to store sesame oil!

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.370
So buy one yourself.

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:46.620
Meow?

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:48.870
This feels familiar somehow.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:52.780
I feel like I spoke freely with someone

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:55.250
like this before, a long time ago...

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:57.440
I don't remember it, though.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.250
That must've been some friend,

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:03.680
to keep up with your incoherent babble.

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:05.180
Friend?

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:08.390
You can only do that with friends, right?

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.630
Actually, wasn't it Uri-tan?

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:13.720
Me?

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:17.110
Yeah! You're my friend, Uri-tan!

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:20.400
No, I'm not your friend, Nya-tan.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:24.320
I'm just an acquaintance you see often.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.500
No way!

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:29.050
Just kidding.

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:32.500
C'mon, you scared me!

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.040
So this is where you are.

00:11:42.230 --> 00:11:43.550
I've been looking for you.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.490
Who's that?

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:51.060
<b>[Maid Café Eto] A café in Akihabara where all the Eto-shin work. 
The manager's mysterious power gives the Eto-shin the appearance 
of cute young ladies, as per the customers' preferences. 
Strange, isn't it?</b>

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:56.020
<b>[The Zodiac Precepts] Laws created for the divine 
ritual of the Eto-shin Selection Festival (ETM12). 
All participating Eto-musume must agree to them
as they are the tournament rules. 
The ETM12 Executive Committee administers them.</b>

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.040
Chu-tan!

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:02.990
Chu-tan?

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.700
She's the rat Eto-shin.

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:08.800
I never dreamed you'd be reincarnated, cat.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:15.910
Nya-tan, are you all right?

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:17.540
What's the big idea, Chu-tan?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.150
The ETM12 is in progress.

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:23.840
Which Eto-musume I battle 
with is my choice.

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:27.170
But it's meaningless for an 
Eto-shin to extend a challenge!

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:28.560
You know that!

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:35.680
Step aside.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:38.570
I cannot allow the cat clan to exist.

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:42.320
I will destroy her.

00:12:42.730 --> 00:12:46.070
Why are you so hostile toward me?

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:48.130
Wh-Why?

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:52.580
You don't remember?

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:55.670
No! But I bet it's a stupid reason!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.510
Like I ate your pudding or something!

00:12:58.350 --> 00:13:01.950
No, I'm quite sure that's not the reason.

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:02.710
Really?!

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:10.380
You haven't forgotten the 
Zodiac Precept that says

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:13.520
we must not harm human beings, have you?!

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.060
I won't kill him.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:21.090
I will only destroy the cat clan.

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:23.070
I'll mutilate you...

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:24.110
Mutilate you...

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:25.500
Mutilate you...

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:26.910
Mutilate you...

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:27.910
Mutilate you...

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:28.780
Mutilate you!

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:29.990
Muscle-ate you!

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.160
Are you that oblivious?!

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.160
<b>Menacing</b>

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:35.290
That one was Nya-tan's fault.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:39.320
Listen to me! You can't fight 
with Chu-tan, no matter what!

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:43.620
It appears you don't remember, 
but she's a dangerous Eto-shin.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:47.300
Let's back off this time.
Run while we hold her off—

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:48.790
Hear me, cat.

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:51.630
If you can defeat me,

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:53.380
I'll make you an Eto-shin immediately.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:54.430
Really?!

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.310
I'll give you my place.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.060
Wait!

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.060
It's my lucky day!

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.150
Nya-tan!

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:02.880
Chu-tan, battle me right now!

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.370
Zodiac Precept No. 40...

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:10.560
When an Eto-musume invokes her 
right to challenge an Eto-shin,

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:13.910
at the moment she accepts the 
terms presented by the Eto-shin,

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.660
the battle for the Sol/Lull Seal 
will automatically begin.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.500
Oh, no!

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:21.840
The battle is on!

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:21.840
<b>Approved</b>

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.340
Etotama! Sol/Lull Charge!

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:24.130
<b>Rat</b>

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:43.100
Rat Eto-shin, Chu-tan!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.940
If it gets dangerous, surrender right away.

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:49.360
Got that, idiot student?

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:50.730
Thanks.

00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:54.240
But I always want to do everything 
in my power to achieve my dream!

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.690
So, since I'm going to battle,

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:58.980
give me some of your awesome 
Sol/Lull, Takeru!

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:02.580
Nya-tan, there's something you 
need to do, isn't there?

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:03.250
Meow?

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:06.000
You haven't apologized 
to them yet, have you?

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:14.330
I said a lot of selfish things today.

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:16.260
I'm sorry!

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:18.310
Also...

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.340
I had fun shopping today.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:23.120
Thanks.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:34.070
Etotama! Sol/Lull Charge!

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:33.570
<b>Cat</b>

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:52.530
Cat Eto-musume, Nya-tan!

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.100
What are your rules?

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:07.110
We fight until

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:08.860
one of us is destroyed.

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:10.870
What?!

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.900
Does she mean until one dies?

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:15.210
That's a hell of a rule she set.

00:16:15.210 --> 00:16:16.370
Nya-tan...

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:24.790
I will wipe you out!

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:08.610
She's ruthless...

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:12.920
Why does Chu-tan hate Nya-tan so much?

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.520
We don't know, either.

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:19.050
It's a fate that has bound rats 
and cats for thousands of years.

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:22.420
Fate? You mean that story about 
the rat tricking the cat

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:25.640
so it couldn't participate in the 
gods' race to join the zodiac?

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:28.480
It's true that the ETM12 of

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:30.700
2,000 years ago was a footrace.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:35.210
And the twelve Zodiac gods chosen 
then were the current twelve.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:38.410
But that means the cat should hate the rat.

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:41.030
Why does Chu-tan hate Nya-tan?

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:46.720
And why did the rat trick the 
cat in the first place?

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:51.550
Do you remember now, cat Eto-musume?

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:55.550
I told you, I don't know 
what you're talking about!

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:04.990
I will destroy you! Destroy you!

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:07.390
Destroy you! Destroy you! 
Destroy you! Destroy you!

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.390
I will destroy you!

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:13.230
Is she going to be okay?

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.070
Nya-tan...

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:19.260
Tell me! How were you reincarnated?

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:20.920
Meow?

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:24.770
I asked you how!

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:35.260
This is bad...

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:39.180
If that's how it is, I'll settle this

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.570
in one blow!

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:43.850
<b>Cat</b>

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:51.280
Cat Gun!

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:51.600
<b>Cat Gun</b>

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.290
No... Impossible...

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:15.460
You have no Sol/Lull left to fight with.

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:17.770
She's in trouble...

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:19.520
Nya-tan...

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:22.550
Uri-tan?

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:25.740
What are you trying to do?

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:29.180
I'm going to intervene in the battle.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:30.520
Intervene?!

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:33.740
Even if you're an Eto-shin, doin' 
somethin' that crazy will mess you up!

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:34.610
Still!

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:37.250
Nya-tan is my friend.

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.210
I can't just keep watching this!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:41.820
Uri-tan...

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:48.200
Uri!

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.910
Etotama! Sol/Lull Charge!

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:50.410
<b>Boar</b>

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:07.470
Boar Eto-shin...

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:09.760
Uri-tan!

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:14.920
Prepare to die, cat Eto-musume!

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:19.030
Nya-tan...

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:21.860
You will exist...

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:31.000
...no more!

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:37.210
Uri-tan!

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:06.780
<b>Void</b>

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:06.780
Wh-What happened?

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:08.210
I dunno.

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:10.870
That's the first time an Eto-shin's

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:12.540
ever intervened in a battle.

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:18.840
We're retreating!

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:31.420
Uri-tan...

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:32.630
Wake up!

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:35.480
Well...

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:38.230
I'm afraid she's gone.

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:40.810
It can't be!

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.450
Uri-tan...

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:47.200
Uri-tan!

00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:50.510
Uri-tan!

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:53.770
What... does this mean?

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:57.090
She's perished.

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:02.140
Uri-tan has perished.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:48.030
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:39.210
Oh, yes! Here's your fortune 
for the year of the beef!

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:41.270
Wait a minute! What do you mean, "beef"?!

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:45.010
A cow fully ripened by her love 
for her honey is called "beef!"

00:23:45.010 --> 00:23:45.960
Shut up, pervert!

00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:48.030
Little kids might grow up thinking 
that's an actual sign!

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:49.800
Next time: Eyes of a Rabbit, 
Ears of a Rabbit.

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>Eyes of a Rabbit, Ears of a Rabbit</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>Boar</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>Goodbye... Yep, Yep.</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>Illustration: Hanamori Yumiri</b>
